{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118592-true-faith","id":1118592,"title":"True Faith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-20T09:27:53-07:00","id":1118592,"title":"True Faith","content":"It is entirely possible that I am unaware of the splat book &quot;True Faith&quot; is covered in (I don't buy the Vampire splats, so I am not up on all the &quot;additional&quot; rules for V:tR beyond the base book), but I was wondering if/how &quot;True Faith&quot; is handled in CoD. I would think it should be fairly simple, but I am hoping there is a mechanic somewhere, even it's a home-brew mechanic.<br /> <br /> Any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13210-fossmano1","name":"FossMaNo1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T09:31:55-07:00","id":1118594,"title":"","content":"I am not sure that I have seen any representation of True Faith in the Chronicles... Though I could have missed it. I do not have all the books.<br /> However there are books from Masquerade that handle True Faith to one degree or another. I am, sadly, AFB currently, so I do not have any actual reference names handy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T09:43:59-07:00","id":1118596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FossMaNo1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118592-true-faith#post1118592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is entirely possible that I am unaware of the splat book &amp;quot;True Faith&amp;quot; is covered in (I don't buy the Vampire splats, so I am not up on all the &amp;quot;additional&amp;quot; rules for V:tR beyond the base book), but I was wondering if/how &amp;quot;True Faith&amp;quot; is handled in CoD. I would think it should be fairly simple, but I am hoping there is a mechanic somewhere, even it's a home-brew mechanic.<br /> <br /> Any ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is more a World of Darkness thing, not a Chronicles of Darkness thing.<br /> <br /> Hunter: the Reckoning instead of Hunter: the Vigil. Though I think people have attempted conversions here before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T10:16:02-07:00","id":1118601,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... I wonder why it hasn't been addressed. Granted, True Faith should be extremely rare (even more rare than any of the Supernatural themselves!), but used correctly for dramatic purposes it could be a very cool NPC plot device. As Vent0 implied (I think), perhaps True Faith philosophically doesn't fit into the CoD cosmology?<br /> <br /> Wait a sec... may be it's because of the whole &quot;God Machine&quot; part of the game (which I don't use as an active plot in my own Chronicles). If I understand the &quot;God machine&quot; correctly, in this cosmology there is no &quot;God,&quot; and so without God there can be no power behind a person of faith. The &quot;God Machine&quot; simply makes religion yet another philosophy to live by.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13210-fossmano1","name":"FossMaNo1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T10:26:22-07:00","id":1118608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118592-true-faith?p=1118596#post1118596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that is more a World of Darkness thing, not a Chronicles of Darkness thing.<br /> <br /> Hunter: the Reckoning instead of Hunter: the Vigil. Though I think people have attempted conversions here before.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what I've seen of miracles have boiled down to ST fiat miracles with a neater name and some word count dedicate to it (mainly about how to procure it and lose it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T10:45:30-07:00","id":1118616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FossMaNo1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118592-true-faith?p=1118601#post1118601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... I wonder why it hasn't been addressed. Granted, True Faith should be extremely rare (even more rare than any of the Supernatural themselves!), but used correctly for dramatic purposes it could be a very cool NPC plot device. As Vent0 implied (I think), perhaps True Faith philosophically doesn't fit into the CoD cosmology?<br /> <br /> Wait a sec... may be it's because of the whole &quot;God Machine&quot; part of the game (which I don't use as an active plot in my own Chronicles). If I understand the &quot;God machine&quot; correctly, in this cosmology there is no &quot;God,&quot; and so without God there can be no power behind a person of faith. The &quot;God Machine&quot; simply makes religion yet another philosophy to live by.</div> </div> </div> </div>The God Machine is... a thing, not really an object of worship. It is more of an inscrutable, unknowable eldritch horror that deals with rebellions and malfunctions constantly as it enacts inscrutable designs. Worship of the God-Machine is only as a result of that worship serving some task or if the Storyteller wants to play up the diefic angle just a bit more, but honestly, there's no &quot;faith&quot; involved in its actions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The point of CoD is that there are no concrete answers, atleast, there shouldn't be. In all of the histories of the supernaturals (atleast most of them), a running theme is that while an Apocalpyse or Masquerade game would treat ancient history as being relevant information that influences the modern game... in CoD, those same events would be regarded the same way as we would myths and legends, only relevant if the GM wants them to be. We don't know beyond any reasonable doubt that there was an ancient historical wolf diety all werewolves came from. We don't know if there is a God, but we see beings who might serve the traditional Judeo-Christian god. We do know of an Irem, but the purpose of the Mummies isn't really meant to be defined and most of them have clouded memories. CoD's history is shrouded and elusive, where as WoD's history is storied and long. Having something called the True Faith would be rather pretentious (though maybe in character for some).<br /> <br /> In any event, there are Miracles... Benedictions from Hunter for the Catholics as well as the option to Bless items against the supernatural in both editions of the corebook. These things are left ambigious as to their power source and the Bless item option is generic enough you can make it alreligious if you wanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T10:57:15-07:00","id":1118619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FossMaNo1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118592-true-faith?p=1118601#post1118601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait a sec... may be it's because of the whole &quot;God Machine&quot; part of the game (which I don't use as an active plot in my own Chronicles). If I understand the &quot;God machine&quot; correctly, in this cosmology there is no &quot;God,&quot; and so without God there can be no power behind a person of faith. The &quot;God Machine&quot; simply makes religion yet another philosophy to live by.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are many gods, and Gods, in the Chronicles Setting, the God-Machine is more of a program than an admin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T11:02:34-07:00","id":1118624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118592-true-faith?p=1118619#post1118619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are many gods, and Gods, in the Chronicles Setting, the God-Machine is more of a program than an admin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless it is a program that gave itself admin privileges, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T11:03:55-07:00","id":1118625,"title":"","content":"well, in the WoD, there was a chance that God is dead and True Faith even came from believing in credit cards, as being rich makes you safe from monsters. True Faith wasn't tied to God, but in you own personal faith, and vampires (as damned beings), were wary of any person which had strong faith in something. In CofD, the situation is quit different. It is not about faith and what you think is true, but about your spirit and ability to withstand the horror. Human don't need to believe in some higher power to save them- they need to believe in themselves. This is why Abjuration, the closest analog to True Faith in the CofD, relay on the person's Willpower directly. If you want to have a True Faith like system in the CofD, my recommendation is using the Abjuration system and expand it to other monsters, such as vampires, werewolves, etc. Holy symbols could be treated as bane for certain monsters in terms of Exorcism or Warding. You could easily redskin it to make it less like &quot;mortal sorcery&quot; which works around having faith in your self and actions, and base it around a &quot;True Faith&quot; trait which decides the strength of the exorcist's faith in the Powers that Be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T12:11:19-07:00","id":1118653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FossMaNo1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118592-true-faith?p=1118601#post1118601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... I wonder why it hasn't been addressed. Granted, True Faith should be extremely rare (even more rare than any of the Supernatural themselves!), but used correctly for dramatic purposes it could be a very cool NPC plot device. As Vent0 implied (I think), perhaps True Faith philosophically doesn't fit into the CoD cosmology?<br /> <br /> Wait a sec... may be it's because of the whole &quot;God Machine&quot; part of the game (which I don't use as an active plot in my own Chronicles). If I understand the &quot;God machine&quot; correctly, in this cosmology there is no &quot;God,&quot; and so without God there can be no power behind a person of faith. The &quot;God Machine&quot; simply makes religion yet another philosophy to live by.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Chronicles of Darkness, the supernatural does undoubtedly exist, and there are many supernatural entities of seemingly godlike power, many of which are worshiped by various inhabitants of the setting. Whether or not any of these entities are truly Gods really depends on your definition of God. None of them are omnipotent, omniscient, or omni-present, however. As in real life, if such an entity does exist, its existence can't really be proven or disproven.<br /> <br /> At any rate, the God-Machine bears very little resemblance to what most folks would think of as a God, and its name is something of a misnomer. It is a literal, physical machine, albeit one that Asimov would describe as &quot;sufficiently advanced&quot; in its programming and operation. Its reach is global at the least, and possibly interplanetary, but certainly not universal. It is far from omnipotent or omniscient, certainly. Quite the contrary in fact, it requires inferastructure and agents to carry out its machinations, which can be disrupted by the sabotaging of lynchpins, and its various interests often seem to be in conflict with one another.<br /> <br /> True Faith doesn't work in Chronicles' cosmology not because of a lack of God, but because of the rules that govern reality being based not on belief but on symbolism.<br /> <br /> In World of Darkness, reality operates on consensus. Whatever the majority of people believe with the greatest conviction becomes true. True Faith makes sense in that paradigm because in such a world, having faith in something can literally make it true. In Chronicles of Darkness, however, reality is defined by what are called, in metaphysics, universals; characteristics or qualities that exist independently of the particulars that exhibit them. True Faith doesn't make sense in this context, because no matter how hard one believes in a thing, that belief alone cannot make it so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-20-2017, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T13:08:38-07:00","id":1118675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118592-true-faith?p=1118625#post1118625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is not about faith and what you think is true, but about your spirit and ability to withstand the horror. Human don't need to believe in some higher power to save them- they need to believe in themselves. This is why Abjuration, the closest analog to True Faith in the CofD, relay on the person's Willpower directly. If you want to have a True Faith like system in the CofD, my recommendation is using the Abjuration system and expand it to other monsters, such as vampires, werewolves, etc. Holy symbols could be treated as bane for certain monsters in terms of Exorcism or Warding. You could easily reskin it to make it less like &quot;mortal sorcery&quot; which works around having faith in your self and actions, and base it around a &quot;True Faith&quot; trait which decides the strength of the exorcist's faith in the Powers that Be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to say Abjuration mechanic expanded to Horrors and creatures with a Template.<br /> <br /> Perhaps there could be a Supernatural Merit that adds the mechanic Holy symbols of your faith in your possession are treated as universal Bane in terms of Exorcism or Warding. (By the way great Merit for Mystery Cult Initiations to bestow for faith based Mystery Cults) Possible have it be a variable merit 1 Dot being for a Specific Categories of Ephemeral Beings (Spirits vs Ghosts vs Angels vs Goetia vs ect...), 2 dots being Universal against Ephemeral Beings, and the 3 dot extending it to Horrors and Major Templates. I'd have the merit require an appropriate Virtue reflecting the Faith (Pious, Righteous, Just, Faithful being examples).<br /> <br /> Also to be the advocate for leaving it based on Willpower think of it also as Composure and Resolve represents banishing doubts, thus the ability to believe uninfluenced by worldly distractions and temptations fits perfectly as well with the exact same mechanics.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T14:08:10-07:00","id":1118696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118592-true-faith?p=1118675#post1118675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps there could be a Supernatural Merit that adds the mechanic Holy symbols of your faith in your possession are treated as universal Bane in terms of Exorcism or Warding. (By the way great Merit for Mystery Cult Initiations to bestow for faith based Mystery Cults) Possible have it be a variable merit 1 Dot being for a Specific Categories of Ephemeral Beings (Spirits vs Ghosts vs Angels vs Goetia vs ect...), 2 dots being Universal against Ephemeral Beings, and the 3 dot extending it to Horrors and Major Templates.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be so incredibly powerful for a one dot Merit. And gamebreaking for a 3 dot one, even in a hunter game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T16:22:49-07:00","id":1118749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118592-true-faith?p=1118675#post1118675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was going to say Abjuration mechanic expanded to Horrors and creatures with a Template.<br /> <br /> Perhaps there could be a Supernatural Merit that adds the mechanic Holy symbols of your faith in your possession are treated as universal Bane in terms of Exorcism or Warding. (By the way great Merit for Mystery Cult Initiations to bestow for faith based Mystery Cults) Possible have it be a variable merit 1 Dot being for a Specific Categories of Ephemeral Beings (Spirits vs Ghosts vs Angels vs Goetia vs ect...), 2 dots being Universal against Ephemeral Beings, and the 3 dot extending it to Horrors and Major Templates. I'd have the merit require an appropriate Virtue reflecting the Faith (Pious, Righteous, Just, Faithful being examples).<br /> <br /> Also to be the advocate for leaving it based on Willpower think of it also as Composure and Resolve represents banishing doubts, thus the ability to believe uninfluenced by worldly distractions and temptations fits perfectly as well with the exact same mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd instead make it more 1 category per dot. At most you could have 5, and everything else would be outside your &quot;faith&quot; or whatever schema you are using.<br /> <br /> And I'd probably make it more narrow than &quot;all spirits&quot; or something like that too, but it would depend on the Chronicle, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T04:50:04-07:00","id":1118907,"title":"","content":"&quot;Faith&quot; is a condition, in the Demon Storyteller Guide. It's specifically Faith toward the God-Machine or its diverse manifestation. It's a weakness, not a strenght. This please the (moronic) atheist in me :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T05:03:04-07:00","id":1118910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118592-true-faith?p=1118675#post1118675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps there could be a Supernatural Merit that adds the mechanic Holy symbols of your faith in your possession are treated as universal Bane in terms of Exorcism or Warding. (By the way great Merit for Mystery Cult Initiations to bestow for faith based Mystery Cults) Possible have it be a variable merit 1 Dot being for a Specific Categories of Ephemeral Beings (Spirits vs Ghosts vs Angels vs Goetia vs ect...), 2 dots being Universal against Ephemeral Beings, and the 3 dot extending it to Horrors and Major Templates. I'd have the merit require an appropriate Virtue reflecting the Faith (Pious, Righteous, Just, Faithful being examples).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not exactly what you're describing, but Hurt Locker has rules for using the occult skill to make charms against supernatural creatures. I think it's reasonable to fluff making those as an act of deep faith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>she/her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13652-manic-pixie-dreamcast","name":"Manic Pixie Dreamcast","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13652_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T13:42:25-07:00","id":1120471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118592-true-faith?p=1118696#post1118696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be so incredibly powerful for a one dot Merit. And gamebreaking for a 3 dot one, even in a hunter game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/118283-curses-and-breaking-points?p=118749#post118749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd instead make it more 1 category per dot. At most you could have 5, and everything else would be outside your &quot;faith&quot; or whatever schema you are using.<br /> <br /> And I'd probably make it more narrow than &quot;all spirits&quot; or something like that too, but it would depend on the Chronicle, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have an idea. I am going to cycle a mechanic I set up for my Frailty Chronice to this purpose. The idea is this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader?p=859927#post859927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of using the blanket term of \u2018Essence\u2019 as the universal term for fuel of ephemeral beings existence and abilities they are divided with terms from various splats. Where these terms are the same as those used in a splat they represent a compatibility of fuels sources. Fuel sources that are normally corporeal, such as vitae, are ephemeral while within an ephemeral being...<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Universal changes to of Ephemeral beings</span></b><br /> <br /> Where CoD lists the word &quot;Essence&quot; between pages 124-139 instead &quot;Supernatural Fuel appropriate to the type of Ephemeral being&quot;...<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Changed Numina</span></b><br /> <i>Drain</i> (changed to)<b> Drain</b><br /> The entity can steal Willpower or any Supernatural Fuel Source that they can otherwise stake from ephemeral entities from a material being(chosen at activation). The activation roll is contested by Stamina + Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance, which ever character -entity or target- gains the most success the most successes receives the point of the stolen power per success, while the other loses a like amount.<br /> <br /> <i>Essence </i><i>Thief</i> (Changed to) <b>Varied Appetites</b><br /> The entity may steal a supernatural fuel from one additional type of supernatural fuel used by another type of ephemeral being per purchase of this Numina. This has the side-effects of making the ephemeral being able to perceive and being perceivable by all potential prey, and while the prey may not steal supernatural fuel that it normally can not feed upon, it can attack back and physically interact with an ephemeral being which it is vulnerable to. When devoured the fuel becomes the primary type used by the being possessing this Numina. (Please note while this does give the ability to interest with ephemeral beings in Twilight, it also opens one up to being physically assaulted/killed by those beings, see &quot;Terrors from Beyond&quot;.)</div> </div> </div> </div>And make True Faith a 3 dot Merit which allows Blessed symbols of your Faith in your possession to act as a Universal Bane for purpose of Abjuration, Exorcism and Warding against beings of a particular supernatural fuel type, regardless if corporeal or Ephemeral. This nicely clumps the creatures into types which seem consistent. It may be bought multiple times, each time representing a different supernatural fuel type.<br /> <br /> What is a Blessed symbol? An item that goes through the proper ceremonies as per CofD page 100 equipment creation rules.<br /> <br /> Ghosts/Geist/Kerberos use Plasm, Angels use Mana, Stryx/Tengu use Vitae, Spirit/Idigam use Essence, Sprites/Hobs/True Fae use Glamour, Goetia and Tulpa use Willpower alone. Horrors could likewise be given a supernatural fuel Pool like a major template, which would make it clear which category they fall in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-25-2017, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}